---
import WikiLayout from '../../layouts/WikiLayout.astro';
import { GLOBAL_ENTITY_REGISTRY } from '../../data/database/global-entity-registry';
import { localizedAlternates } from '../../i18n/utils';
import { coreSeoKeywords } from '../../i18n/seo-keywords';
const seoKeywords = coreSeoKeywords('en', 'database');
const groups = [
  { href:'/database/weapons/', name:'Weapons Database', count:GLOBAL_ENTITY_REGISTRY.filter((x)=>x.type==='weapon').length, text:'Weapon roles, observed parameters and linked loadout guidance.' },
  { href:'/database/vehicles/', name:'Vehicles Database', count:GLOBAL_ENTITY_REGISTRY.filter((x)=>x.type==='vehicle').length, text:'Transport, aircraft and armored vehicle reference entries.' },
  { href:'/database/maps/', name:'Maps Database', count:GLOBAL_ENTITY_REGISTRY.filter((x)=>x.type==='map').length, text:'Terrain orientation, map identity and related objective systems.' },
];
---
<WikiLayout title="WARDOGS Game Database" description="Browse the WARDOGS knowledge database for connected weapons, vehicles, maps and battlefield systems." canonicalPath="/database/" pageType="CollectionPage" datasetName="WARDOGS Game Knowledge Database" schemaItems={groups.map((x)=>({name:x.name,url:x.href}))} primaryKeyword={seoKeywords[0]} keywords={seoKeywords.slice(1)} image="/images/database/game-knowledge-database-overview.jpg" imageAlt="WARDOGS knowledge database with weapon, vehicle and terrain reference panels" imageWidth={2164} imageHeight={727} alternates={localizedAlternates('database')} xDefaultPath="/database/">
  <div class="database-hero"><p class="eyebrow">GAME KNOWLEDGE DATABASE</p><h1>WARDOGS Database</h1><p>A structured index of version-bound game entities, parameters, relationships and patch history. Start with a collection, then follow entity links into guides and related systems.</p></div>
  <figure class="knowledge-hero-media"><img src="/images/database/game-knowledge-database-overview.jpg" alt="Illustrated WARDOGS knowledge database with weapon, vehicle and terrain reference panels" width="2164" height="727" loading="lazy" decoding="async" fetchpriority="low" /><figcaption>Database records connect equipment, vehicles and terrain concepts without inventing unsupported game values.</figcaption></figure>
  <section><h2>How the database is organized</h2><p>Each collection is a controlled entry point into the same knowledge graph. Entity records identify what an item is, summarize its battlefield role, show the parameters that can be supported, and connect it to relevant comparisons and guides. This structure is designed for quick lookups without separating a fact from the context needed to use it.</p><p>The current database reflects the documented Season 1 / Patch 0.11 snapshot. Values that have not been established by a reliable source are shown as <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong>. That label is deliberate: the database does not convert community assumptions into official statistics.</p></section>
  <section class="database-hub-grid">{groups.map((group)=><a href={group.href}><span>{group.count}</span><strong>{group.name}</strong><small>{group.text}</small></a>)}</section>
  <section><h2>Explore connected data</h2><div class="inline-link-row"><a href="/equipment/">Equipment</a><a href="/factions/">Factions</a><a href="/game-modes/">Game modes</a><a href="/tools/">Interactive tools</a></div></section>
  <section><h2>Database workflow</h2><ol><li>Choose the weapon, vehicle or map collection.</li><li>Open an entity record for its overview and current parameters.</li><li>Follow relation links to comparisons, guides and associated systems.</li><li>Check patch history before relying on version-sensitive information.</li></ol><p>For practical decisions, pair the database with the <a href="/tools/">interactive tools</a>. The tools help narrow a choice, while entity pages preserve the evidence and limitations behind it.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Does the database contain every hidden statistic?</h3><p>No. Unsupported values remain <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong> until they can be documented responsibly.</p><h3>Are database entries the same as guides?</h3><p>No. Entries organize entity facts and relationships. Guides such as <a href="/how-to-play/">How To Play</a> explain how systems work together in a match.</p><h3>How often does the database change?</h3><p>Records are version-bound and reviewed when documented patches affect the associated entity or system.</p></section>
</WikiLayout>
